diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 28fbc56..e8a57b8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -291,6 +291,21 @@ # ~/.config/plannotator-tui/config.toml
 `cursor` and `selection` become plain backgrounds when set: the text on them keeps the
 terminal's colour.
 
+Fenced code is syntax-highlighted when `[ui] code_theme` names a TextMate theme:
+
+```toml
+[ui]
+code_theme = "~/.config/plannotator-tui/tokyonight_night.tmTheme"
+```
+
+`~/` is your home folder, and any other relative path is read from the folder the config
+file is in. The theme is read once at startup. A file that cannot be read or is not a
+TextMate theme is an error that names it, reported by `plannotator-tui config`; the review
+itself still opens, with plain code. Only a fence whose language is recognised is
+highlighted, in the theme's colours; other fences and indented code use `code-block`.
+Without `code_theme` nothing is highlighted, and a fence's opening line shows its backticks
+without the language name.
+
 On a wide terminal, `[ui]` can keep the text to a readable measure:
 
 ```toml
